PROJECT: Cardano

## Ecosystem Position

Primary Sector: Layer 1 Blockchain / Smart Contract Platform
Secondary Sector: Proof-of-Stake Infrastructure / Decentralized Governance / DeFi & NFT Platform / Enterprise Identity (Atala PRISM)
Primary Chain: Cardano Mainnet
Supported Chains: Cardano Mainnet; Testnet Preprod; Testnet Preview; Midnight Partner Chain (Polkadot SDK, ZK privacy); Milkomeda C1 (EVM sidechain, community-operated); Ergo (cross-chain research collaborations)
Sources: (HIGH) [Cardano Architecture, https://docs.cardano.org/architecture]; (HIGH) [Midnight Network, https://midnight.network/]; (HIGH) [Milkomeda, https://milkomeda.com/]; (MEDIUM) [Cardano Ecosystem Map, https://cardano.org/ecosystem/]

## External Dependencies

Dependency Name: Ouroboros Consensus Research (Academic Partners)
Dependency Type: Protocol
Purpose: Formal verification, security proofs, protocol evolution (Praos, Genesis, Leios, Peras) via university partnerships (University of Edinburgh, Tokyo Institute of Technology, University of Athens, others)
Criticality: Critical
Status: Live
Related Entity: Input Output Global (IOG)
Related Technology Component: Ouroboros Consensus Protocol Family
Sources: (HIGH) [IOG Research Library, https://iohk.io/en/research/library/]; (HIGH) [IOG Academic Partners, https://inputoutput.io/academic-partners/]

Dependency Name: Haskell Compiler (GHC) & Toolchain
Dependency Type: SDK
Purpose: Core protocol implementation (cardano-node, cardano-ledger, ouroboros-consensus, plutus-core) compiled with GHC; runtime dependency
Criticality: Critical
Status: Live
Related Entity: Input Output Global (IOG)
Related Technology Component: Current Technical Stack (Runtime)
Sources: (HIGH) [IOG GitHub cardano-node, https://github.com/input-output-hk/cardano-node]; (HIGH) [GHC Official, https://www.haskell.org/ghc/]

Dependency Name: Nix Package Manager (Reproducible Builds)
Dependency Type: Infrastructure
Purpose: Reproducible builds for cardano-node, tooling, and CI/CD pipelines across IOG and community operators
Criticality: High
Status: Live
Related Entity: Input Output Global (IOG)
Related Technology Component: Current Technical Stack (CI/CD)
Sources: (HIGH) [IOG GitHub Nix Config, https://github.com/input-output-hk/iohk-nix]; (MEDIUM) [NixOS, https://nixos.org/]

Dependency Name: Cloud Providers (AWS, GCP, Azure, DigitalOcean, Hetzner, OVH)
Dependency Type: Cloud
Purpose: Hosting for Blockfrost API, Koios API, Ogmios/Kupo indexers, many SPO block producers, relay nodes, and developer infrastructure
Criticality: High
Status: Live
Related Entity: Blockfrost; Koios; Stake Pool Operators (various)
Related Technology Component: API Layer; P2P Layer
Sources: (MEDIUM) [Blockfrost Infrastructure, https://blockfrost.io/]; (MEDIUM) [Koios Deployment, https://github.com/cardano-community/koios-artifacts]; (MEDIUM) [SPO Cloud Survey 2023, https://cardano-community.github.io/guild-operators/]

Dependency Name: Verifiable Random Function (VRF) Cryptography (libsodium / cardano-crypto)
Dependency Type: Security
Purpose: Leader election in Ouroboros Praos; stake-proportional, private, unpredictable slot leadership
Criticality: Critical
Status: Live
Related Entity: Input Output Global (IOG)
Related Technology Component: Consensus Mechanism (Leader Election)
Sources: (HIGH) [IOG Research Ouroboros VRF, https://iohk.io/en/research/library/]; (HIGH) [cardano-crypto GitHub, https://github.com/input-output-hk/cardano-crypto]

Dependency Name: BLS12-381 Curve Libraries (for Midnight ZK)
Dependency Type: Protocol
Purpose: Zero-knowledge proof system (ZK-SNARKs) for Midnight partner chain; pairing-based cryptography
Criticality: High (for Midnight)
Status: Live (Midnight devnet/testnet)
Related Entity: Input Output Global (IOG) / Midnight Team
Related Technology Component: Midnight Partner Chain
Sources: (HIGH) [Midnight Docs Cryptography, https://docs.midnight.network/]; (MEDIUM) [blst Library, https://github.com/supranational/blst]

Dependency Name: Polkadot SDK (Substrate Framework)
Dependency Type: Protocol
Purpose: Midnight partner chain built on Polkadot SDK for sovereign chain with shared security model
Criticality: High (for Midnight)
Status: Live (Midnight devnet/testnet)
Related Entity: Input Output Global (IOG) / Midnight Team
Related Technology Component: Midnight Partner Chain
Sources: (HIGH) [Midnight Announcement Polkadot SDK, https://iohk.io/en/blog/posts/2022/11/18/introducing-midnight/]; (HIGH) [Polkadot SDK, https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk]

Dependency Name: CBOR (Concise Binary Object Representation) Libraries
Dependency Type: Protocol
Purpose: Serialization format for all on-chain data structures (blocks, transactions, scripts, certificates)
Criticality: Critical
Status: Live
Related Entity: Input Output Global (IOG)
Related Technology Component: Current Technical Stack (Serialization)
Sources: (HIGH) [Cardano Spec CBOR, https://github.com/input-output-hk/cardano-ledger/blob/master/eras/shelley/impl/src/Cardano/Ledger/Binary/Cbor.hs]; (HIGH) [RFC 8949 CBOR, https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8949]

Dependency Name: Ed25519 / Blake2b-256 Cryptographic Primitives
Dependency Type: Security
Purpose: Key generation, signing, hashing for all on-chain operations (UTxO, staking, governance)
Criticality: Critical
Status: Live
Related Entity: Input Output Global (IOG)
Related Technology Component: Security Model (Cryptography)
Sources: (HIGH) [cardano-crypto GitHub, https://github.com/input-output-hk/cardano-crypto]; (HIGH) [RFC 8032 Ed25519, https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8032]

Dependency Name: Diffie-Hellman Key Exchange / TLS (P2P Networking)
Dependency Type: Protocol
Purpose: Secure peer-to-peer communication between cardano-nodes (Diffusion layer with pipelining)
Criticality: High
Status: Live
Related Entity: Input Output Global (IOG)
Related Technology Component: P2P Layer
Sources: (HIGH) [Ouroboros Network Framework, https://github.com/input-output-hk/ouroboros-network]

Dependency Name: LLVM / WASM Toolchains (for Aiken, Helios, Cardano Serialization Lib)
Dependency Type: SDK
Purpose: Compilation targets for alternative smart contract languages (Aiken → Plutus Core via WASM/LLVM; Helios browser compilation; CSL Rust/WASM bindings)
Criticality: Medium
Status: Live
Related Entity: Aiken Team; Helios Team; MeshJS/CSL Maintainers
Related Technology Component: Development Framework (SDK)
Sources: (HIGH) [Aiken Compiler Architecture, https://aiken-lang.org/]; (HIGH) [Helios Compiler, https://helios-lang.io/]; (HIGH) [Cardano Serialization Lib, https://github.com/Emurgo/cardano-serialization-lib]

Dependency Name: GitHub Actions / GitLab CI (CI/CD Platforms)
Dependency Type: Infrastructure
Purpose: Automated testing, building, and deployment for core repositories (IOG, Cardano Foundation, Emurgo, community projects)
Criticality: Medium
Status: Live
Related Entity: Input Output Global (IOG); Cardano Foundation; Emurgo; Community Projects
Related Technology Component: Current Technical Stack (CI/CD)
Sources: (MEDIUM) [IOG GitHub Actions Workflows, https://github.com/input-output-hk/cardano-node/tree/master/.github/workflows]; (MEDIUM) [Cardano Foundation CI, https://github.com/CardanoFoundation/CIPs/tree/master/.github/workflows]

Dependency Name: Discourse / IdeaScale (Governance Platforms)
Dependency Type: Service
Purpose: Project Catalyst proposal submission, discussion, and voting (IdeaScale); CIP discussion (Discourse/GitHub)
Criticality: High (for governance operations)
Status: Live
Related Entity: Cardano Foundation; Project Catalyst
Related Technology Component: Project Catalyst; CIP Process
Sources: (HIGH) [Project Catalyst IdeaScale, https://cardano.ideascale.com/]; (HIGH) [CIP Discourse, https://github.com/cardano-foundation/CIPs/discussions]

Dependency Name: Docker / Container Orchestration (Kubernetes, k3s)
Dependency Type: Infrastructure
Purpose: Containerized deployment for cardano-node, Ogmios, Kupo, Blockfrost, Koios, and SPO infrastructure
Criticality: High
Status: Live
Related Entity: Blockfrost; Koios; SPO Community; IOG
Related Technology Component: API Layer; P2P Layer
Sources: (MEDIUM) [Blockfrost Docker, https://docs.blockfrost.io/#section/Running-locally/Docker]; (MEDIUM) [Koios Docker, https://github.com/cardano-community/koios-artifacts/tree/main/docker]; (MEDIUM) [Guild Operators Docker, https://github.com/cardano-community/guild-operators/tree/master/scripts/cnode-helper-scripts]

## Major Integrations

Integration Name: Milkomeda C1 (EVM Sidechain)
Integrated With: Milkomeda Protocol (dcSpark)
Purpose: EVM compatibility for Cardano; allows Solidity smart contracts to settle on Cardano via wrapped ADA (milkADA) and bridged assets
Status: Live
Related Historical Event ID: EV-028 (Pertumbuhan Ekosistem DeFi - cross-chain composability)
Sources: (HIGH) [Milkomeda Documentation, https://milkomeda.com/]; (MEDIUM) [Milkomeda Bridge, https://milkomeda.com/bridge]

Integration Name: Wanchain Bridge (Cross-chain to Ethereum, BSC, Polygon, etc.)
Integrated With: Wanchain
Purpose: Decentralized cross-chain bridge for ADA and native assets to/from EVM chains via secure multiparty computation (sMPC)
Status: Live
Related Historical Event ID: EV-028 (Pertumbuhan Ekosistem DeFi - cross-chain liquidity)
Sources: (HIGH) [Wanchain Cardano Bridge, https://www.wanchain.org/cardano/]; (MEDIUM) [Wanchain Docs, https://docs.wanchain.org/]

Integration Name: cBridge (Celer Network)
Integrated With: Celer Network
Purpose: Fast cross-chain transfers for native assets and stablecoins between Cardano and 30+ EVM chains
Status: Live
Related Historical Event ID: EV-028 (Pertumbuhan Ekosistem DeFi)
Sources: (HIGH) [Celer cBridge Cardano, https://cbridge.celer.network/]; (MEDIUM) [Celer Network Blog, https://blog.celer.network/]

Integration Name: Chainlink Price Feeds (via Charli3/Orcfax Oracle Integration)
Integrated With: Chainlink (data source) / Charli3 / Orcfax (native oracle networks)
Purpose: Chainlink data aggregated by Charli3 and Orcfax for on-chain DeFi consumption; not direct Chainlink VRF/CCIP on Cardano mainnet
Status: Live (via native oracle networks)
Related Historical Event ID: EV-028 (Pertumbuhan Ekosistem DeFi - oracle infrastructure)
Sources: (HIGH) [Charli3 Chainlink Integration, https://charli3.io/]; (HIGH) [Orcfax Data Sources, https://orcfax.io/]; (MEDIUM) [Chainlink Blog Cardano, https://blog.chain.link/]

Integration Name: Atala PRISM + Government Identity Systems (Ethiopia, Georgia, Tanzania)
Integrated With: Ministry of Education Ethiopia; Ministry of Justice Georgia; Tanzania Government
Purpose: National-scale DID and verifiable credentials deployment for student credentials, document verification, and digital identity
Status: Live (pilot/production phases)
Related Historical Event ID: EV-027 (Peluncuran Atala PRISM Mainnet); EV-031 (Cardano Summit 2022 Nation-State Partnerships)
Sources: (HIGH) [Atala PRISM Ethiopia Case Study, https://atalaprism.io/case-studies/ethiopia/]; (HIGH) [Atala PRISM Georgia Case Study, https://atalaprism.io/case-studies/georgia/]; (MEDIUM) [IOG Blog Ethiopia, https://iohk.io/en/blog/posts/2021/04/29/atala-prism-mainnet-launch/]

Integration Name: Firefly Wallet + Ledger / Trezor Hardware Wallets
Integrated With: Ledger; Trezor
Purpose: Hardware wallet support for ADA and native assets via Firefly (IOG) / native support in Daedalus, Yoroi, Lace, Eternl, Vespr, Typhon
Status: Live
Related Historical Event ID: EV-009 (Yoroi Launch); EV-010 (Daedalus Flight); EV-020 (Lace Launch)
Sources: (HIGH) [Ledger Cardano Support, https://support.ledger.com/hc/en-us/articles/4404379573905-Cardano-ADA]; (HIGH) [Trezor Cardano Support, https://wiki.trezor.io/Cryptocurrencies#Cardano]; (HIGH) [Lace Hardware Wallet, https://lace.io/]

Integration Name: WalletConnect v2 (Multi-wallet dApp Connection Standard)
Integrated With: WalletConnect Foundation
Purpose: Universal wallet connection protocol for Cardano dApps (CIP-30 + WalletConnect v2 support in Lace, Eternl, Vespr, Typhon, Nami, Yoroi)
Status: Live
Related Historical Event ID: EV-030 (Infrastruktur Developer Matang)
Sources: (HIGH) [WalletConnect Cardano, https://walletconnect.com/]; (MEDIUM) [CIP-30 Spec, https://cips.cardano.org/cips/cip30/]

Integration Name: Bitcoin Bridge Research (Trust-minimized BTC-ADA Bridge)
Integrated With: Bitcoin Network (via research collaboration)
Purpose: Research on trust-minimized bridge between Bitcoin and Cardano using cryptographic commitments (IOG research paper "Non-Interactive Proof-of-Work" and follow-ups)
Status: Planned / Research
Related Historical Event ID: EV-035 (Penelitian Akademis 100+ Papers - cross-chain research)
Sources: (HIGH) [IOG Research Bitcoin Bridge, https://iohk.io/en/research/library/]; (MEDIUM) [IOG Blog Bitcoin Sidechain, https://iohk.io/en/blog/posts/2022/06/14/bitcoin-sidechains/]

Integration Name: Ergo (Sigma Protocols & Cross-chain DeFi Research)
Integrated With: Ergo Platform
Purpose: Shared research on sigma protocols, non-interactive zero-knowledge proofs, and cross-chain DeFi primitives (IOG researchers collaborate with Ergo core team)
Status: Live (research collaboration)
Related Historical Event ID: EV-035 (Penelitian Akademis - cross-chain cryptography)
Sources: (HIGH) [Ergo-Cardano Research, https://ergoplatform.org/en/blog/]; (MEDIUM) [IOG Blog Ergo, https://iohk.io/en/blog/posts/2021/06/14/ergo-cardano/]

Integration Name: World Mobile Token (WMT) / EarthNodes on Cardano
Integrated With: World Mobile Chain (partner chain initiative)
Purpose: Telecom infrastructure token using Cardano for settlement and staking; EarthNodes operate on Cardano-adjacent infrastructure
Status: Live
Related Historical Event ID: EV-028 (Pertumbuhan Ekosistem - Real World Assets)
Sources: (HIGH) [World Mobile Token, https://worldmobiletoken.com/]; (MEDIUM) [Cardano Summit WMT, https://cardanosummit.io/]

## Infrastructure Providers

Provider: Blockfrost
Service: REST API, WebSocket, IPFS Gateway, dedicated nodes, webhook, analytics for Cardano mainnet/preprod/preview
Criticality: Critical (primary hosted API provider for majority of dApps)
Status: Live
Sources: (HIGH) [Blockfrost Website, https://blockfrost.io/]; (HIGH) [Blockfrost Docs, https://docs.blockfrost.io/]

Provider: Koios
Service: High-performance REST API, SQL access, historical data, light-weight indexer for Cardano (community-operated, open-source)
Criticality: High (major alternative to Blockfrost; used by many analytics tools)
Status: Live
Sources: (HIGH) [Koios Website, https://koios.rest/]; (HIGH) [Koios GitHub, https://github.com/cardano-community/koios-artifacts]

Provider: Ogmios
Service: WebSocket JSON-RPC interface to local cardano-node for transaction submission and chain sync (self-hosted)
Criticality: High (standard local node interface for dApp backends)
Status: Live
Sources: (HIGH) [Ogmios Website, https://ogmios.dev/]; (HIGH) [Ogmios GitHub, https://github.com/CardanoSolutions/ogmios]

Provider: Kupo
Service: Lightweight chain indexer with pattern-matching UTxO queries (SQLite backend) for dApp state synchronization
Criticality: High (widely used with Ogmios for local indexing)
Status: Live
Sources: (HIGH) [Kupo GitHub, https://github.com/CardanoSolutions/kupo]; (HIGH) [Kupo Docs, https://kupo.cardanosolutions.io/]

Provider: MeshJS
Service: TypeScript/JavaScript SDK for dApp development (wallet connection, transaction building, Plutus interaction, off-chain code)
Criticality: High (most adopted TS SDK)
Status: Live
Sources: (HIGH) [MeshJS Website, https://meshjs.dev/]; (HIGH) [MeshJS GitHub, https://github.com/MeshJS/mesh]

Provider: Lucid
Service: TypeScript/Deno library for transaction building, off-chain code, and Plutus script interaction (alternative to MeshJS)
Criticality: High (popular alternative SDK)
Status: Live
Sources: (HIGH) [Lucid GitHub, https://github.com/spacebudz/lucid]; (HIGH) [Lucid Docs, https://lucid.spacebudz.io/]

Provider: Aiken
Service: ML-inspired smart contract language, compiler, LSP, package manager, testing framework for Plutus Core
Criticality: High (leading alternative to Plutus Tx/Haskell)
Status: Live
Sources: (HIGH) [Aiken Website, https://aiken-lang.org/]; (HIGH) [Aiken GitHub, https://github.com/aiken-lang/aiken]

Provider: Helios
Service: JavaScript-like language for Plutus Core, browser-based IDE, compiler, testing framework
Criticality: Medium (growing adoption for web-native developers)
Status: Live
Sources: (HIGH) [Helios Website, https://helios-lang.io/]; (HIGH) [Helios GitHub, https://github.com/Hyperion-BT/helios]

Provider: Cardano Serialization Library (CSL)
Service: Rust/WASM/JS bindings for low-level transaction serialization, signing, and cryptographic operations
Criticality: Critical (foundational library used by almost all wallets and SDKs)
Status: Live
Sources: (HIGH) [CSL GitHub, https://github.com/Emurgo/cardano-serialization-lib]; (HIGH) [CSL Docs, https://emurgo.github.io/cardano-serialization-lib/]

Provider: Dandelion / cardano-node (P2P Network)
Service: Reference implementation of cardano-node (Haskell) running Diffusion/Pipelining P2P layer (CIP-31)
Criticality: Critical (sole production consensus client)
Status: Live
Sources: (HIGH) [cardano-node GitHub, https://github.com/input-output-hk/cardano-node]; (HIGH) [CIP-31 Pipelining, https://cips.cardano.org/cips/cip31/]

Provider: Mithril Network (Aggregators & Signers)
Service: Stake-based threshold multi-signature aggregators for certified snapshots (fast sync, light clients, governance tally)
Criticality: High (enables light clients and fast bootstrap)
Status: Live (IOG-operated aggregators; community signer network)
Sources: (HIGH) [Mithril Network, https://mithril.network/]; (HIGH) [Mithril Docs, https://mithril.network/doc/]

Provider: Charli3 Oracle Network
Service: Decentralized oracle network providing price feeds and external data to Cardano DeFi via incentivized node operators
Criticality: High (primary native oracle for DeFi)
Status: Live
Sources: (HIGH) [Charli3 Website, https://charli3.io/]; (HIGH) [Charli3 Docs, https://docs.charli3.io/]

Provider: Orcfax Oracle Network
Service: Fact-based oracle network with auditability and data integrity focus for Cardano DeFi
Criticality: High (second major native oracle)
Status: Live
Sources: (HIGH) [Orcfax Website, https://orcfax.io/]; (HIGH) [Orcfax Docs, https://docs.orcfax.io/]

Provider: TxPipe / Pallas (Rust Implementation)
Service: Rust implementation of Cardano protocols (node components, ledger, networking) — alternative client development
Criticality: Medium (experimental alternative client)
Status: Live (development)
Sources: (HIGH) [TxPipe GitHub, https://github.com/txpipe]; (HIGH) [Pallas GitHub, https://github.com/txpipe/pallas]

